{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Procedural Mesh Extrusion and Subdivision.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Procedural Mesh Extrusion and Subdivision.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"procedural mesh extrusion and subdivision procedural mesh extrusion and subdivision","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Procedural Mesh Extrusion and Subdivision.md","fileName":"Procedural Mesh Extrusion and Subdivision.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Procedural Mesh Extrusion and Subdivision","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Procedural Mesh Editing with bmesh]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Procedural Mesh Editing with bmesh","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Procedural Mesh Extrusion and Subdivision.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Procedural Mesh Extrusion and Subdivision.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"procedural mesh extrusion and subdivision procedural mesh extrusion and subdivision","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Procedural Mesh Extrusion and Subdivision.md","fileName":"Procedural Mesh Extrusion and Subdivision.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Procedural Mesh Extrusion and Subdivision","heading":"Procedural Mesh Extrusion and Subdivision","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Extrusion creates new connected geometry from a selected region, while subdivision inserts additional components into existing topology. In scripted modeling, these operations turn a simple primitive into a structure whose complexity is controlled by parameters rather than manual edits.\n\nA useful sequence selects components by a reproducible characteristic, subdivides or extrudes them, and then transforms the new region. Because each operation changes the topology and may change indices, later stages should re